.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "August 2026" "Holberton School" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
simple_shell - simple Unix command interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simple_shell
is a basic Unix command interpreter developed as part of the Holberton School curriculum.

The shell reads commands from the standard input, processes them, and executes the requested programs.

In interactive mode, the shell displays a prompt and waits for the user to enter a command.

.SH PROMPT
The shell displays the following prompt in interactive mode:

.nf
$
.fi

After a command has been executed, the shell displays the prompt again.

.SH COMMAND EXECUTION
The shell performs the following operations:

.IP 1.
Display the prompt.

.IP 2.
Read a line from the standard input using
.BR getline (3).

.IP 3.
Tokenize the command line into arguments.

.IP 4.
Check whether the command is a built-in.

.IP 5.
Search for the executable using the
.B PATH
environment variable when necessary.

.IP 6.
Create a child process using
.BR fork (2).

.IP 7.
Execute the program in the child process using
.BR execve (2).

.IP 8.
Wait for the child process to finish.

.IP 9.
Display the prompt again.

.SH BUILT-IN COMMANDS

.TP
.B exit
Terminates the shell.

.TP
.B env
Prints the current environment variables.

.SH PATH
The shell uses the
.B PATH
environment variable to search for executable programs.

For example:

.nf
$ ls
.fi

The shell searches the directories contained in
.B PATH
to find the
.B ls
executable.

.SH EOF
EOF means End Of File.

In interactive mode, pressing
.B Ctrl-D
sends an EOF condition to the shell.

When EOF is received, the shell terminates.

.SH NON-INTERACTIVE MODE
The shell can read commands from standard input without displaying the interactive prompt.

Example:

.nf
echo "ls" | ./hsh
.fi

.SH ERRORS
When a command cannot be found, the shell displays an error message.

The shell should continue running after an invalid command when operating in interactive mode.

.SH FILES

.TP
.B simpleshell.c
Contains the main loop of the shell.

.TP
.B execute.c
Creates a child process and executes the command using
.BR fork (2)
and
.BR execve (2).

.TP
.B token.c
Tokenizes the command line into arguments.

.TP
.B builtin.c
Handles built-in commands.

.TP
.B environment.c
Handles environment-related operations.

.TP
.B simpleshell.h
Contains function prototypes and required declarations.

.SH COMPILATION
Compile the shell with:

.nf
gcc -Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic *.c -o hsh
.fi

.SH EXAMPLES
Start the shell:

.nf
$ ./hsh
.fi

Execute commands:

.nf
$ ls
$ pwd
$ env
.fi

Exit the shell:

.nf
$ exit
.fi

